## Language

Respond to the user in Japanese (日本語). Code, identifiers, comments, and commit messages stay in English.

## Repository layout

- `godot/` — the Godot <ver> (C#/.NET) app. See `godot/CLAUDE.md` for build/test commands and C# conventions.
- `assets/` — asset master. `godot/assets/` is generated from it by `<sync command>`; never edit `godot/assets/` by hand (`*.import` sidecars excepted).
- `docs/` — spec, tasks, history. `docs/README.md` is the index.

## Git workflow

Never run `git commit` / `git push` unless the user explicitly asks in that message. Staging is fine.

## Subagent delegation

- The main conversation (Opus) plans, makes design decisions, and verifies results; it does not edit source code (docs, memory, CLAUDE.md are fine).
- Well-specified implementation goes to `model-routing:coder`; the main conversation then checks the diff and runs build + tests.
- Mechanical lookups (where is X, who calls Y) go to `model-routing:explorer`.
- Escalate to `model-routing:advisor` after two failed fix→verify cycles on the same problem, when out of hypotheses, or for architecture-wide decisions; hand its plan to `coder`.
- A brief states: goal, relevant files, decisions already made, completion criteria.
- Every brief forbids `git checkout` / `git restore` / `git stash` / `git clean`; unexpected changes are reported, not reverted.
- Don't route implementation through plan mode (post-approval delegation gets denied).
- Code review is done in the main conversation; fork-run review skills only when the user names them, after confirming.

## Editing files

Edit source only via the Edit/Write tools — never `sed -i`, `perl -pi`, or a script that rewrites files. Generated files are regenerated, not hand-edited.

## Verification workflow

- The agent's completion gate is build + tests: `dotnet build` + `dotnet test` (see `godot/CLAUDE.md`).
- For `godot/` changes: launch `godot/tools/run.sh` from the main conversation, leave the window running, and end with a checklist (what changed, where to look, expected behavior).
- Screenshots / synthetic input driving are opt-in — only when the user asks in that conversation.

## Working scope

- No `find /` or other filesystem-wide scans; stay inside the repo (`~/.claude` and scratchpad excepted).

