# CLAUDE.md (godot/)

## Project layout

- `MyGame.csproj` — the Godot app (`Godot.NET.Sdk`, `InvariantGlobalization=true`, `<Compile Remove="lib/**/*.cs" />` + `tools/**`). `Autoload/GameApp.cs` is the only Autoload. `run/main_scene` is `Scenes/Title.tscn`.
- `lib/MyGame.Core/` — Godot-independent logic (`IsAotCompatible=true`).
- `lib/MyGame.Core.Tests/` — xUnit, no Godot reference; excluded from ExportDebug/ExportRelease.
- `lib/` and `tools/` have `.gdignore`.

## Environment

- Godot <ver> .NET at `/Applications/Godot_mono.app`. `/usr/local/bin/godot` must be a wrapper script that `exec`s the real binary — a symlink breaks GodotSharp resolution.
- Export templates for <ver>.stable.mono must be installed separately after every editor upgrade.
- iOS: `xcode-select` must point at Xcode.app; close Xcode before `export.sh iOS`.

## Commands

- `dotnet build godot/MyGame.sln -m:1 -nodeReuse:false --disable-build-servers` — build (flags required inside the sandbox).
- `dotnet test godot/lib/MyGame.Core.Tests/MyGame.Core.Tests.csproj -m:1 -nodeReuse:false --disable-build-servers --no-build` — tests (run alone with the sandbox disabled: vstest binds loopback; `--no-build` keeps build/restore inside the sandbox).
- `godot --headless --path godot --import` — run after asset/import-setting changes; build first on a fresh checkout.
- `godot/tools/run.sh` — build → import → launch.
- `godot/tools/export.sh <iOS|macOS> [debug|release]` — build → import → export → iOS signing patch.
- Only `dotnet test --no-build`, `godot`, `run.sh`, and `export.sh` run with the sandbox disabled, each as a standalone command (never chained with `&&`). Everything else, including `dotnet build`, stays sandboxed. Ask before adding third-party addons or NuGet packages (they run unsandboxed via the editor/tests).

## C# conventions

- Game logic lives in Core; engine handles come in through small Core-side interfaces.
- Randomness is injected (`IRandomSource`), never a static call.
- JSON only through source-generated `JsonSerializerContext` (NativeAOT trimming).
- Bundled data loaders throw on failure; user-data loaders (`user://`) fall back to defaults.
- UI is built inside `UiFrame` (fixed design space fitted into `SafeArea`); backgrounds stay outside it; modals own their frame.
- Late-shown root Controls size via `FitToViewport()`, never `SetAnchorsPreset()`.
- All Controls `FocusMode = None` (text `LineEdit`s: `Click` + release before any modal).
- Tap handlers accept only `InputEventScreenTouch { Pressed: true, Index: 0 }`; modal backdrops dismiss on release.
- Fonts are imported as MSDF.
- <Add engine quirks here with the reason and how they were found.>

## Testing discipline

Core logic gets real xUnit tests. Godot-bound scene code is verified by the user on a launched build — the agent builds, tests, launches `run.sh`, and hands over a checklist.
